# Story 10: Tabs Overview (45s)
# Hook: Tabs hold panes, panes hold agents -- and switching between them is one keystroke.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-010-tabs-overview.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
Tabs hold panes, panes hold agents -- and switching between tabs is one keystroke.

[00:05.0 --> 00:13.0]
Start rysh and you get one tab with one pane. That's your starting point.

[00:13.0 --> 00:22.0]
Let's add a tab so we have something to move between -- Ctrl+T, then n.

[00:22.0 --> 00:32.0]
The bracket keys move between tabs: left bracket for previous, right bracket for next.

[00:32.0 --> 00:45.0]
Alt plus the left and right arrows do the same thing. Each tab is its own workspace of panes and agents.

